{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l23fw88t","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"group-17-elements-halogen-family","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pbleaching-powder-contains-a-salt-of-an-oxoacid-as-one-of-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-pcw6k8t5iktndnrq","content":"<p>Bleaching powder contains a salt of an oxoacid as one of its components. The anhydride of that oxoacid is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Cl<sub>2</sub>O"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Cl<sub>2</sub>O<sub>7</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"ClO<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Cl<sub>2</sub>O<sub>6</sub>"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>Bleaching powder is CaOCl<sub>2</sub> which contains HOCl as an oxoacid and the anhydride of which is Cl<sub>2</sub>O.</p>"}]}